 Betting Personality Beats Intelligence", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-20", "d": "Oct 20"}, {"t": "The AI vs AI Battle for the Internet", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-22", "d": "Oct 22"}]}, {"lab": "a", "model": "Claude Opus 5.5", "notes": ["Claude Duet: waitlisted personal‑agent preview built on Opus 5.5", "NLW bets Duet is prelude to Fable 5.5 before the IPO", "Opus 5.5 tops AA’s new imagination index"], "eps": [{"t": "Why AI Companies Are Betting Personality Beats Intelligence", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-20", "d": "Oct 20"}, {"t": "The AI vs AI Battle for the Internet", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-22", "d": "Oct 22"}]}, {"lab": "g", "model": "Gemini 4 Argon", "notes": ["Argon scores highest on AA’s new “slop” personality index", "Coding verdicts still split; writing & multimodal standouts", "Only major lab without a personal agent, per NLW"], "eps": [{"t": "Why AI Companies Are Betting Personality Beats Intelligence", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-20", "d": "Oct 20"}, {"t": "What Gemini 4 Argon Is Actually Good For", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-14", "d": "Oct 14"}]}], "harness": [["Claude Code", "Anthropic", ">$2.5B", "run‑rate · Feb (official)", "Claude"], ["Cursor", "Anysphere", "~$4B", "annualized · Jun (reported)", "Own: Composer 2 (Kimi K2.5 base)"], ["Codex", "OpenAI", "5M+", "weekly users · Jun (official)", "GPT"], ["Devin / Windsurf", "Cognition", "~$1B", "run‑rate · late Sep (reported)", "Own: SWE‑2"], ["Lovable", "Lovable", ">$600M", "ARR · Sep (TechCrunch)", "Claude Opus 5.5 / Fable 5.1"], ["Replit", "Replit", "~$525M", "ARR · Apr (estimate)", "Multi: Fable 5.x, GPT‑6 Astra"], ["OpenClaw", "OpenClaw Fdn", "392k ★", "GitHub stars · Oct 18", "Any (bring your own)"], ["Hermes Agent", "Nous Research", "255k ★", "GitHub stars · Oct 18", "Any + own Hermes 4"], ["v0", "Vercel", "6M+", "users · Mar (reported)", "—"], ["Bolt.new", "StackBlitz", "$40M", "ARR · Mar 2025 (old)", "Mostly Claude (reported)"]], "matrix": {"cols": ["Claude", "GPT", "Gemini", "Grok", "Chinese open", "Local", "Own model"], "rows": [["Claude Code", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Codex", "", "●", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Cursor", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "", "● Composer 2"], ["Devin / Windsurf", "○", "○", "○", "", "", "", "● SWE‑2"], ["Lovable", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Replit", "●", "●", "", "", "", "", ""], ["OpenClaw", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", ""], ["Hermes Agent", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "● Hermes 4"], ["Perplexity", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "", "● Sonar"], ["Bolt.new", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""]]}, "coverage": {"All sections": "curated by hand for the Oct 25 edition from live sources (see links)"}, "caveats": ["Unlock % are Grok Bot estimates from access tier, harness, effort defaults and habits, anchored on Anthropic's Claude Code study (novice ~15% vs expert ~28–33% verified success). No cross‑lab study measures this.", "Moved since Oct 18: Kimi K3.1 Pro enters the capability overhang chart (AA 55) at an estimated researcher 60–75 / everyday 15–30: strong API and Kimi Code access but a top‑up is needed to unlock it, weights aren't out yet, and Western consumer reach is small. Google (Argon) and Meta (Muse Wonder) ratings unchanged from Oct 18. Earlier moves (Sep 21 → Oct 12): OpenAI everyday 30–45, Anthropic researcher 70–85.", "Usage: ChatGPT >1.2B weekly (OpenAI); Gemini app >1B monthly (Google, Aug); Grok ~117M monthly AI‑feature users (SpaceX S‑1, Mar); Claude app ~56M monthly (Reuters/Sensor Tower, Jun). Mobile DAU figures via BofA/Sensor Tower are secondary. Codex + Work \"40M active\" has no stated window.", "Argon intro pricing $2/$10 until Nov 30, then $4/$20. 3.8 Flash $0.75/$3.75; Astra $10/$50. Grok 4.6‑high #66 · 1456 on Arena. Claude Haiku 5.5 (Oct 7, $0.10/$0.50) joined Text Arena Oct 22 at #126 · 1425 and scores AA 43.", "AI Daily Brief notes paraphrase Nathaniel Whittemore’s episode transcripts (aidailybrief.ai, Sep 22 – Oct 23), incl. reactions he quoted; commentary, not data. This week: Oct 20 (AA personality benchmark: Opus 5.5 tops imagination, Argon tops slop, Dots feel dry), Oct 21 (Muse 10M US downloads in 40 days, Tesla Grok), Oct 22 (Claude Duet, PHP2Shell and AI‑vs‑AI cyber). No AIDB episode on Kimi K3.1 Pro yet.", "Full landscape (Oct 25): one row per company's latest/best model. Arena = LMArena Text Oct 22 (418 models); AA = Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index Oct 25 (best effort setting). Kimi K3.1 Pro (Oct 23, 2.8T/104B active, $2/$10) scores AA 55, #4 behind Opus 5.5 58 and Sonnet 5.5 / Muse Wonder Full 56; AA counts it proprietary until Moonshot publishes weights (promised by Nov 4), when it would cut the open‑vs‑closed AA gap from 12 to 3. It is not on Text Arena yet (Kimi K3 still #18 · 1487). Moonshot says it filtered cyber data out of training (its own, unverified 81% vs 90.5% cyber score). MiniMax M3.1 Flash (Oct 19, $0.15/$0.60) scores AA 43 with weights 'later'; not on Text Arena. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 now has an AA score (45, up from 39); its Arena figure is the 0910 build (#34 · 1476). Reflection Beam 1.0 (501B/23B active, Apache 2.0, Oct 16) is #104 · 1436 on Arena and AA 30. Meta Muse Spark Open still not on Text Arena. Mistral Large 4 is a proprietary preview. Microsoft MAI‑Thinking‑1, ByteDance Seed, Baidu ERNIE AA, Perplexity Sonar and SSI have no public text‑leaderboard score. Coding Agent % for Kimi, GLM‑5.3, Qwen3.8 Max and Step 5 come from AA's Coding Agent Index (various harnesses); none yet for K3.1 Pro.", "SSI: still no model, paper or API as of Oct 25; $32B valuation (Apr 2025 round) and ~$5B Nvidia investment (Jul 27, Bloomberg‑reported size). Rumoured August model did not ship. Thinking Machines: Inkling (975B/41B active, open weights, Jul 15) + Tinker fine‑tuning platform. Perplexity retired Sonar Chat Completions Sep 27; Agent API routes to OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, Z.AI, Moonshot, NVIDIA plus Sonar. ARR >$450M (Mar, FT via secondary tracker). Perplexity this week: open‑sourced its SPACE agent sandbox and brought Computer to Valarian's air‑gapped infrastructure (Oct 20).", "Harness figures are mixed quality: official = Claude Code >$2.5B run‑rate (Feb 12), Codex 5M+ weekly (Jun 2). Secondhand/estimates = Cursor ~$4B (Jun), Cognition ~$1B (Sep), Replit ~$525M (Apr), v0 6M+ users, OpenClaw 3.2M MAU (SimilarWeb est.). Claude Code ~$15B “tracked ARR” is a third‑party estimate, not shown. Lovable >$600M ARR via TechCrunch. Bolt $40M is Mar 2025, no newer figure. Lovable/Bolt model stacks are third‑party reporting. Hermes = Nous Research’s Hermes Agent (open source) + Hermes 4 models.", "Capability overhang: ceiling = AA Intelligence; reach = ceiling × midpoint of unlock estimate. Kimi K3.1 Pro (60–75/15–30) replaces MiMo‑V2.6 in the top six. Meta Muse Wonder (60–75/30–45) and Kimi are derived estimates.", "xAI: no new text model; Grok 5 was previewed Oct 14 with no release date and the API still tops out at grok‑4.7 (a third‑party roundup claiming an Oct 19 Grok 5 launch is not backed by x.ai or docs.x.ai). OpenAI: no new text model; Decisions API on GPT‑6 Luna went GA Oct 22, OpenAI models are coming to Google Cloud (Oct 21), and GPT‑6 Astra was pitched for COBOL/Fortran migration (Oct 19). Google: Agent Compute Engine announced Oct 22; Pichai says Gemini 5 will surpass Argon. Anthropic: Claude Duet research preview Oct 21 (US Pro/Max, waitlist).", "Vendor benchmark tables treated as claims; LMArena and Artificial Analysis are independent."], "links": [{"t": "x.ai Grok 4.7", "url": "https://x.ai/news/grok-4-7"}, {"t": "docs.x.ai", "url": "https://docs.x.ai/developers/grok-4-7"}, {"t": "GPT‑6.1 Sol", "url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-1-sol"}, {"t": "Sol docs", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol"}, {"t": "GPT‑6 for everyone", "url": "https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-for-everyone/"}, {"t": "DevDay recap", "url": "https://openai.com/index/devday-2026-recap/"